reference=[('Question ownership', 'Claude generates the questions and options. The host can add an Other control to its own UI without modifying the original questions array. Questions invented by the application belong in a separate application flow.'), ('Answer shape', 'Use full question text as each key, not the short header. The app joins multi-select labels with comma-space, which the SDK supports. Custom Other text is a per-question answer; response is a general reply replacing the structured answer list.'), ('Question and preview limits', 'The question tool supports one to four questions and two to four options per question. Preview fields are optional. The configured format applies to the session but does not guarantee a preview for every option.'), ('HTML preview boundaries', 'The SDK rejects script, style elements and DOCTYPE in generated HTML previews. This UI also sanitizes allowed tags and attributes, uses a sandbox without scripts and applies a content policy that blocks external resources. Trusted wrapper CSS keeps preview text readable.'), ('Plan mode', 'The plan experiment asks an actual clarifying question before a short read-only plan. It exposes only Read and AskUserQuestion and never enables edits. A model-generated plan artifact, if attempted by the runtime, remains outside the permitted tool scope and is logged.'), ('Waiting versus deferred execution', 'This app keeps a process alive while the callback promise waits. A two-minute timeout cancels and settles it. The documented PreToolUse defer pattern is a separate design for resuming persisted sessions and is explained here without pretending it is implemented.'), ('Local teaching scope', 'The loopback server accepts one active query and checks POST origins. Request IDs are single-use; invalid or stale decisions cannot approve another request. A deployed multi-user app needs authenticated ownership and its own durable lifecycle.'), ('Evidence and API usage', 'All questions, previews and native results in the live examples come from actual SDK calls. Scripted CLI/test selections are labelled explicitly. Each query has a $0.45 SDK budget threshold, not a prepaid cap. Credentials, dependencies and all teaching media stay outside Git.')]
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Every architecture step has source-linked coloured code.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 31 · Clarifying questions\n\nFive linked student pages, large text, actual SDK experiments and coloured code in all thirteen UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson31-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson31-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson31-clarifying-questions`. Open http://127.0.0.1:3131 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+, API credit and model access are required. Windows may require Git Bash.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file. Enter your own model key, then restart. Existing shell values take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nNo GitHub token or Managed Agents IDs are required. Secrets, dependencies and teaching media stay outside Git.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, selected lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\n## References\n\n- [Official SDK approvals documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/user-input)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`. Run `npm test` for offline boundaries, review lifecycle, workspace and startup checks.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 31 pages and thirteen source-linked UML steps.')
